========================================================================
  VERIFICATION 2: SCALING LAW OCR(n) ~ 1 - c/n
========================================================================

  n | 1-OCR    | n*(1-OCR) | Notes
  --+----------+-----------+------
  3 | 0.000000 | 0.0000    | degenerate
  4 | 0.000000 | 0.0000    | degenerate
  5 | 0.052632 | 0.2632    | 
  6 | 0.076923 | 0.4615    | 
  7 | 0.084054 | 0.5884    | 

  VERDICT: The 1-c/n scaling is based on ONLY 3 non-degenerate points
  (n=5,6,7). n*(1-OCR) = 0.26, 0.46, 0.59 — NOT constant!
  The deficit is GROWING, not stabilizing.
  Better fit: 1-OCR ~ a/n + b for some a,b, or a*log(n)/n

  Fit 1 (c/n): c=0.4377, SSE=0.00169766
  Fit 2 (a+b/n): a=0.1665, b=-0.5614, SSE=0.00002348
  Fit 3 (c*ln(n)/n): c=0.2412, SSE=0.00093829

  With only 3 data points, ALL fits are equally valid.
  The scaling law is UNDERDETERMINED. Need n=8,9,10 data.

