    H|scores-entropy = 1.2805 bits
    Mutual information I(H; scores) = 2.7697 bits
    Fraction of H-info captured = 0.6838

========================================================================
  VERIFICATION 8: Linear model quality at n=6
========================================================================

  Linear model: H ≈ 45.0000 + (-3.0000) × S₂
  R² = 0.923077
  Mean |residual| = 2.6367
  Max |residual| = 8.5000
  Max H = 45
  Max relative error = 18.9%

  Quadratic model: H ≈ 51.0268 + (-4.8214)×S₂ + (0.107143)×S₂²
  Quadratic R² = 0.947802
  Quadratic max |residual| = 9.2500

  Multi-regression: H ≈ 0.5542 + (-0.4602)×S₂ + (5.0795)×c₃
  Multi R² = 0.923077
  Multi max |residual| = 8.5000

  KEY CHECK: Is c3 determined by the score sequence?
  At n=6: 0/22 score classes have multiple c3 values
  c3 IS determined by scores (Rao's formula)! Multi-regression gains nothing new.
  c3 = C(n,3) - sum(s_i*(s_i-1)/2)

========================================================================
  VERIFICATION 9: How many distinct invariants to determine H?
========================================================================

  By OCF: H = I(Omega(T), 2) = 1 + 2*alpha_1 + 4*alpha_2 + ...
  H is EXACTLY determined by the conflict graph Omega(T).
  Question: What is the MINIMAL set of symmetric invariants?

