========================================================================
  SYNTHESIS: WHAT THE SHADOW COMPRESSION ACTUALLY IS
========================================================================

  CONFIRMED CLAIMS:
    ✓ OCR(n) ≈ 0.92-0.95 for n=5,6,7 (S₂ explains 92-95% of H variance)
    ✓ Score determines H perfectly at n=3,4
    ✓ (scores, c3, c5) determines H exactly at n=5
    ✓ Completeness is necessary: OCR drops with sparsity
    ✓ Compression ratio grows with n

  CLAIMS NEEDING QUALIFICATION:
    ? OCR ~ 1-c/n scaling: based on only 3 non-degenerate points
    ? 'Recovery improves with n': no verified OCR beyond n=7
    ? 'c3 adds information': c3 = f(scores) by Rao's formula (no new info)
    ? The n≥20 OCR extrapolations (95%, 98%, 99%) are UNVERIFIED

  KEY INSIGHT (maybe the most important one):
    The shadow is NOT a lossy compression of the tournament.
    It is a lossy compression of H.
    The tournament has 2^{n(n-1)/2} states.
    The score sequence partitions these into ~n^{n-1} classes.
    Within each class, H varies by at most ~8% at n=5-7.
    The STRUCTURAL question is: does this 8% shrink, grow, or stabilize?

